completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Given [the following code](https://getpsalm.org/r/bbf4881e60):\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n\r\nclass Session\r\n{\r\n    /** @var array */\r\n    private $sessionData;\r\n\r\n    /**\r\n     * @param array $sessionData\r\n     */\r\n    private function __construct(array $sessionData)\r\n    {\r\n        $this->sessionData = $sessionData;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    /**\r\n     * @param array $data\r\n     *\r\n     * @return Session\r\n     */\r\n    public static function fromData(array  $data): self\r\n    {\r\n        return new static($data);\r\n    }\r\n}  \r\n\r\nclass SessionProvider\r\n{\r\n    /** @var Session|null */\r\n    private static $session = null;\r\n\r\n    /**\r\n     * @return Session\r\n     */\r\n    public function getSession(): Session\r\n    {\r\n        // This line generates the issue\r\n        return self::$session ?? self::$session = Session::fromData($_SESSION ?? []);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nMixedArgument - 36:69 - Argument 1 of Session::fromData cannot be mixed, expecting array<array-key, mixed>\r\n```\r\n\r\nStrange thing here is that both `$_SESSION` and `[]` as arguments don't generate the same issue.\r\n\r\nI've tried finding the issue myself, but couldn't in a reasonable amount of time. If it's fixed, I'll try to learn something from that commit.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance!","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":